    <section class="nova-buy__guide" aria-label="Professional dental implant buying guide">
      <aside><span>In this guide</span><a href="#buying-online">Buying online</a><a href="#component-families">Component families</a><a href="#why-nova">Why NOVA</a><a href="#digital-workflow">Digital workflows</a><a href="#bulk-orders">Clinic &amp; laboratory orders</a><a href="#delivery-support">Delivery &amp; support</a></aside>
      <div class="nova-buy__guide-content">
        <section id="buying-online"><span class="nova-kicker">Buying dental implants online</span><h2>Professional purchasing starts with verification.</h2><p>Online access makes implant procurement faster, but the purchasing decision remains clinical and system-specific. Before selecting an implant or restorative component, identify the intended system, connection geometry, platform, dimensions and treatment workflow. A similar appearance or product name is not evidence of compatibility.</p><p>NOVA gives clinics and laboratories a connected catalog with visible product references and supporting documentation. Product pages and collection filters help narrow the selection; the current label, catalog reference and applicable Instructions for Use remain the authority for the final decision.</p><div class="nova-buy__callout"><strong>Professional ordering principle</strong><p>Choose the system first, then confirm every component in the restorative stack before placing the order.</p></div></section>
        <section id="component-families"><span class="nova-kicker">System overview</span><h2>NOVA implant and restorative component families.</h2><h3>PSI implant systems</h3><p>The NOVA catalog presents the PSI family as a tapered internal-hex implant system available across multiple diameters and lengths. Select the exact configuration required for the treatment plan and verify the current product labeling before use.</p><h3>Healing and restorative components</h3><p>Healing abutments, straight and angled abutments, temporary solutions and related prosthetic components support the transition from implant placement to restoration. Match connection, platform, gingival height and restorative design.</p><h3>Impression and laboratory components</h3><p>Transfers, analogs and casting components help reproduce the implant position for conventional laboratory workflows. Confirm open- or closed-tray technique and the matching system reference.</p><h3>Multi-unit and overdenture workflows</h3><p>Multi-unit and attachment components support full-arch and removable restorative planning. Review angulation, cuff height, restorative interface and the associated screws or accessories as one connected group.</p><h3>Digital and CAD/CAM components</h3><p>Digital components support scan, design and restorative production workflows. Physical compatibility and the corresponding digital library must both match the selected implant platform.</p></section>
        <section id="why-nova"><span class="nova-kicker">Manufacturer documentation</span><h2>Why professionals choose a documented system.</h2><div class="nova-buy__reasons"><article><b>01</b><strong>Connected catalog</strong><p>Implant, healing, restorative, impression, digital and surgical references are organized as one professional workflow.</p></article><article><b>02</b><strong>Regulatory transparency</strong><p>Review the official FDA K150363 record and the authentic ISO 13485:2016 certificate directly on the site.</p></article><article><b>03</b><strong>Reference-led selection</strong><p>Catalog numbers and dimensions help teams communicate precisely between clinic, laboratory and purchasing staff.</p></article><article><b>04</b><strong>Direct product support</strong><p>Contact NOVA when a connection, configuration or catalog reference needs clarification before ordering.</p></article></div></section>
        <section id="digital-workflow"><span class="nova-kicker">Digital dentistry</span><h2>Connect the physical component to the digital plan.</h2><p>Digital implant workflows depend on consistent geometry from scan through final restoration. When selecting scan bodies, Ti-bases or related CAD/CAM components, confirm the implant connection, restorative platform and the correct digital library together.</p><p>This verification chain helps the clinic and laboratory preserve alignment between the planned restoration and the physical interface. If the required library or compatibility statement is unclear, contact NOVA before design or production begins.</p><a class="nova-buy__inline-link" href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/digital-cad-cam-casting">Explore digital components <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section>
        <section id="bulk-orders"><span class="nova-kicker">Clinic and laboratory procurement</span><h2>Prepare repeat and multi-item orders efficiently.</h2><p>Practices and laboratories managing multiple cases can use Quick Order to search product names and catalog references, select configurations and assemble several items in one working view. Standardizing around confirmed component families can simplify purchasing and reduce avoidable selection errors.</p><p>For larger requirements, recurring needs or assistance organizing a system-level order, contact NOVA with the known platform and catalog references. Product availability, pricing and suitability should be confirmed for the specific order.</p><div class="nova-buy__split-actions"><a href="/pages/quick-order">Open Quick Order <span>→</span></a><a href="/pages/contact">Discuss a larger order <span>→</span></a></div></section>
        <section id="delivery-support"><span class="nova-kicker">From order to delivery</span><h2>Shipping information and professional support.</h2><p>Accurate account, contact and delivery details help the NOVA team process an order efficiently. Available shipping services, costs and estimated delivery times are listed on the Shipping &amp; Delivery page. Timing is an estimate and may vary by inventory, destination, carrier and order review.</p><p>For urgent case requirements, confirm availability and dispatch expectations with NOVA before relying on a delivery date. Tracking information should be used to monitor the shipment after dispatch.</p><a class="nova-buy__inline-link" href="/pages/shipping-delivery">Review shipping &amp; delivery <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section>
